<title>UK: NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil seen up.</title>
<headline>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil seen up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil prices were notionally steady to firmer on Monday but dealers said limited activity made prices hard to assess.</p>
<p>One trader said he thought the rise in crude prices may have pushed levels up to around $140 fob NWE.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
</text>
